Package: spdeST
Title: SPDE Smoothing and RKHS Covariance Tests for Spatial Features
Version: 0.0.1.9081
Authors@R: person(given = "Yihe", family = "Yang",
    email = "yxy1234@case.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Provides topology-aware boundary learning and finite-element mesh
    generation, a proper Matern stochastic partial differential equation
    smooth registered with 'mgcv', and signed reproducing-kernel Hilbert space
    covariance score tests for spatial and spatiotemporal feature pairs. A
    score scan selects the spatial features, a sparse Laplace REML fit of the
    Poisson or negative-binomial SPDE model estimates them, and a sparse score
    kernel with a signed quadratic-form saddlepoint calibration tests their
    pairs. WGCNA module analysis uses the pairwise estimate of the latent spatial
    correlation, the score divided by its information, within explicitly
    selected feature blocks.
